# A text message-passing channel between concurrent tasks: the portable communication default (message passing over shared memory). The clean uniform interface; each backend wraps its platform channel (node async queue, rust tokio mpsc, swift buffered queue, kotlin BlockingQueue) behind this API, selected at build time. The platform channel lives in the opaque `dock` handle, typed per backend. send / receive are async; a buffered channel holds a value sent before receive is called, so send-then-receive never races.

load @term/base/code/native/channel
  find do-make
  find do-send
  find do-receive
  find do-close

# a channel carrying text messages
form channel
  link dock, like channel-handle

  # send a message (buffered; never blocks for an unbounded channel)
  task send
    note async
    take self
    take item, like text
    like void
    call do-send
      read self
      read item
      wait true

  # receive the next message, waiting if none is buffered yet
  task receive
    note async
    take self
    like text
    send back
      call do-receive
        read self
        wait true

  # close the channel
  task close
    note async
    take self
    like void
    call do-close
      read self
      wait true

# make a new text channel
task make-channel
  like channel
  send back
    make channel
      bind dock
        call do-make
